{% set local_problem %}
<p>Hampton Cove homes often have substantial roofs that collect significant rainwater during storms. That water needs somewhere to go — and where it goes matters. Downspouts that dump water too close to the foundation cause erosion, moisture intrusion, and foundation damage over time.</p>

<p>Many builder-installed downspouts weren't designed with Hampton Cove's landscaping in mind. They discharge onto carefully designed beds, wash out mulch, and create erosion problems. Proper downspout design considers the whole picture — moving water safely away from the foundation and landscaping.</p>

<p>For many Hampton Cove homeowners, underground downspout extensions provide the best solution: water moves far from the foundation through invisible buried pipes.</p>
{% endset %}

